I go to the empty ticket counter.
A clerk is sitting there.
"Hello madam," he says.
"Hello brother, I need one ticket," I say.
I give him one hundred rupees.
He gives me a pass.
"Here is your ticket," he says.
I ask him a question.
"Are those upstairs galleries open right now?"
"Yes madam, they are open," the clerk says.
"But you go into this main hall."
He points to the right.
"That hall is very beautiful," he tells me.
"Thank you," I say, and I go inside.
This building is very big and quiet.
Outside, the sound of the rain is very loud.
But here, there is absolute silence.
A few minutes ago, I was on a noisy street.
Now this place feels completely different.
